 "api_error_status": null,
 "result": "Rules are deferred on the bundle and replayed onto the app at registration.\n\n1. **Recording (`src/tessel/sansio/bundles.py`)**\n   - `Bundle.attach_route_rule` (~line 413) validates the endpoint and view name, then calls `self.record(lambda s: s.attach_route_rule(...))`.\n   - `Bundle.record` (~224) appends the lambda to `Bundle.deferred_functions`.\n   - Nothing touches the app yet.\n\n2. **Registration**\n   - `App.register_bundle` (`src/tessel/sansio/app.py:571`) calls `bundle.register(self, options)` (line 596).\n   - `Bundle.register` (`sansio/bundles.py:273`) builds a `BundleSetupState` via `make_setup_state` (~246).\n   - It then loops `for deferred in self.deferred_functions: deferred(state)` (~334).\n   - In the same method (~324) it also calls `state.attach_route_rule(...)` for the bundle's static route.\n\n3. **Applying the rule**\n   - `BundleSetupState.attach_route_rule` (`sansio/bundles.py:87`) applies the `url_prefix` and `subdomain`.\n   - It merges the URL defaults and prefixes the endpoint with `name_prefix.bundle_name.`.\n   - It then calls `app.attach_route_rule(...)` (`sansio/app.py:606`), which adds the rule to the app's URL map.",
